1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,288
Last time, the ruin kept a secret.

2
00:00:02,738 --> 00:00:04,997
Today, it has a story.

3
00:00:05,897 --> 00:00:08,896
There are four steps, one after another,

4
00:00:09,346 --> 00:00:11,184
each in a different part of the ruin.

5
00:00:12,084 --> 00:00:15,504
The crew is paid for each one, and the last one ends the game.

6
00:00:17,304 --> 00:00:19,323
And I didn't open the story file once.

7
00:00:20,523 --> 00:00:23,302
There's a shipped campaign made of ruins like this one.

8
00:00:24,202 --> 00:00:26,237
Each ruin in it is one episode,

9
00:00:26,687 --> 00:00:29,046
and every episode is the same chain.

10
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:33,711
First the approach, where the crew comes up to the way in.

11
00:00:34,161 --> 00:00:36,312
Then a call, from somebody who knows the place.

12
00:00:37,212 --> 00:00:39,530
Then a room, and a call, and a room.

13
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:42,019
And at the end comes the piece,

14
00:00:42,469 --> 00:00:45,028
where they take away what the ruin was hiding.

15
00:00:46,828 --> 00:00:50,322
You can already write every link in that chain.

16
00:00:51,222 --> 00:00:54,127
What's new today is where the last word comes from.

17
00:00:54,577 --> 00:00:56,261
Nobody can leave the ship yet,

18
00:00:56,711 --> 00:00:58,802
so today, Comms says it.

19
00:01:00,002 --> 00:01:01,575
The story needs a heading,

20
00:01:02,025 --> 00:01:04,818
and I put it below the last quest in the section.

21
00:01:05,718 --> 00:01:07,777
It's an arc, with three hashes,

22
00:01:08,227 --> 00:01:11,326
and the word Arc alone on the first line.

23
00:01:12,226 --> 00:01:15,121
It starts at once, and it fails after twenty minutes.

24
00:01:16,021 --> 00:01:18,199
There's a Win sentence for when it's finished,

25
00:01:18,649 --> 00:01:21,428
and a Lose sentence for when it fails.

26
00:01:23,228 --> 00:01:24,896
All of that is Class 1.

27
00:01:25,796 --> 00:01:27,135
The description's a page,

28
00:01:27,585 --> 00:01:29,848
so it gets three short paragraphs.

29
00:01:30,748 --> 00:01:33,528
First the station, drawn beside its own line,

30
00:01:33,978 --> 00:01:35,733
so the crew knows who's sending them.

31
00:01:36,633 --> 00:01:38,596
Then what's known about the markers.

32
00:01:39,496 --> 00:01:42,085
Nobody warns the crew about the clock,

33
00:01:42,535 --> 00:01:46,165
so the last paragraph says twenty minutes,

34
00:01:46,615 --> 00:01:48,685
and that the haze is closing in.

35
00:01:49,885 --> 00:01:50,725
Here's the first step.

36
00:01:51,175 --> 00:01:54,050
It has four hashes, so it belongs to the arc.

37
00:01:54,950 --> 00:01:58,107
And this is the line that matters:

38
00:01:58,557 --> 00:02:01,278
done when, reach entrance, one thousand.

39
00:02:03,078 --> 00:02:07,518
Before, I wrote that sentence in a Starts when line, to start a beat.

40
00:02:08,418 --> 00:02:12,038
Here it's in a Done when line, so it finishes a step.

41
00:02:12,938 --> 00:02:14,385
The rules haven't changed.

42
00:02:14,835 --> 00:02:18,295
Entrance is a role, the word on the place's Roles line.

43
00:02:19,195 --> 00:02:21,225
This place's key is way in,

44
00:02:21,675 --> 00:02:24,943
and the key doesn't work here. Lint will tell you.

45
00:02:26,742 --> 00:02:30,201
A thousand is how close, and always write the number.

46
00:02:31,101 --> 00:02:33,347
Without it the game uses five thousand,

47
00:02:33,797 --> 00:02:36,702
and the step is finished before the crew has seen the ruin.

48
00:02:37,602 --> 00:02:40,255
One more thing, for numbers inside a ruin:

49
00:02:40,705 --> 00:02:42,866
the game looks every two seconds,

50
00:02:43,316 --> 00:02:46,418
so don't go below about three hundred.

51
00:02:47,618 --> 00:02:48,781
Now two more steps.

52
00:02:49,681 --> 00:02:52,904
Both say starts when, revealed, so they're asleep.

53
00:02:53,804 --> 00:02:55,820
The way in reveals the first,

54
00:02:56,270 --> 00:02:58,822
and the first reveals the second.

55
00:02:59,722 --> 00:03:01,681
It's the full address every time:

56
00:03:02,131 --> 00:03:04,521
the arc, a slash, the step.

57
00:03:06,321 --> 00:03:07,359
Now look at this.

58
00:03:07,809 --> 00:03:10,982
Reach altar, six hundred, is in my file twice.

59
00:03:11,882 --> 00:03:13,602
On the beat, it starts the call.

60
00:03:14,052 --> 00:03:16,072
On the step, it finishes the step.

61
00:03:16,972 --> 00:03:19,723
They happen together, when the ship comes into the Vault:

62
00:03:20,173 --> 00:03:22,772
the step is done, and Rook is on Comms.

63
00:03:24,572 --> 00:03:28,662
The second step sends the ship to the Niche, the place I hid.

64
00:03:29,562 --> 00:03:31,857
The crew can find it because Rook tells them,

65
00:03:32,307 --> 00:03:34,102
or because they go and look.

66
00:03:35,002 --> 00:03:37,274
So if Comms shuts the recording off,

67
00:03:37,724 --> 00:03:39,663
the story can still be finished.

68
00:03:40,863 --> 00:03:44,075
The last step is the piece, where somebody takes the thing.

69
00:03:44,975 --> 00:03:46,832
Nobody can leave the ship today,

70
00:03:47,282 --> 00:03:49,953
so this is a decision Comms makes.

71
00:03:50,853 --> 00:03:54,463
The step says done when, signal, hollow taken.

72
00:03:54,913 --> 00:03:57,402
It waits for a word, and that word is mine.

73
00:03:58,302 --> 00:03:59,651
And it has an Action:

74
00:04:00,101 --> 00:04:03,732
the moment the step starts, Rook calls with a second recording.

75
00:04:05,532 --> 00:04:06,543
Now for the scene.

76
00:04:07,443 --> 00:04:10,832
One answer asks what it is, and leads to a second scene.

77
00:04:11,282 --> 00:04:13,437
The other says take it aboard,

78
00:04:13,887 --> 00:04:16,441
and after the semicolon, it sends the word.

79
00:04:17,341 --> 00:04:19,478
The step hears it and pays,

80
00:04:19,928 --> 00:04:22,892
and it was the last step, so the game is won.

81
00:04:24,692 --> 00:04:27,002
Look at the ways out of this conversation.

82
00:04:27,452 --> 00:04:30,108
There are two, and both send the word.

83
00:04:31,008 --> 00:04:32,359
I did that on purpose.

84
00:04:33,259 --> 00:04:35,255
If I add an answer that just hangs up,

85
00:04:35,705 --> 00:04:37,701
a crew that picks it has spent the call,

86
00:04:38,151 --> 00:04:40,033
and the step can never be finished.

87
00:04:40,933 --> 00:04:43,658
The crew's way of saying not now is the Back button.

88
00:04:45,458 --> 00:04:48,556
So why a word, and not the way Class 2 did it?

89
00:04:49,456 --> 00:04:52,342
Because the step doesn't care who says the word.

90
00:04:52,792 --> 00:04:55,612
When your crew can go and take the bowl by hand,

91
00:04:56,062 --> 00:04:58,355
this step won't change by one letter.

92
00:04:59,555 --> 00:05:02,502
Two lectures ago I put a Scan line on the Altar.

93
00:05:03,402 --> 00:05:05,120
That's for a person standing there,

94
00:05:05,570 --> 00:05:08,660
and the Science console on the ship doesn't show it.

95
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:14,056
Science reads scan records, the ones from Class 1.

96
00:05:15,856 --> 00:05:17,182
A place wears a role,

97
00:05:17,632 --> 00:05:20,129
and a role is all a scan record needs.

98
00:05:21,029 --> 00:05:25,168
So I write Scan of, the role, a tab, and a reading.

99
00:05:26,068 --> 00:05:28,085
That's one line on the place for a person,

100
00:05:28,535 --> 00:05:30,648
and one record in Scans for the ship.

101
00:05:31,848 --> 00:05:33,856
So I run lint, and it's clean.

102
00:05:34,756 --> 00:05:37,774
Now I use the key where the role goes,

103
00:05:38,224 --> 00:05:41,558
and lint says nothing in this mission wears a role called way in.

104
00:05:42,458 --> 00:05:45,124
That's good, because that step would never have finished.

105
00:05:46,924 --> 00:05:49,324
Next I drop the arc from a reveal line.

106
00:05:49,774 --> 00:05:52,384
Lint tells me what the step is called to the game,

107
00:05:52,834 --> 00:05:55,758
and to write that.

108
00:05:57,558 --> 00:06:01,732
Now I take these two lines off the last step, and lint says clean.

109
00:06:02,632 --> 00:06:03,872
And this one matters.

110
00:06:04,772 --> 00:06:07,257
The other three steps still say they're required,

111
00:06:07,707 --> 00:06:12,536
so the game decides the arc is finished when those three are.

112
00:06:13,436 --> 00:06:16,722
The crew wins at the niche, with the last call still ringing.

113
00:06:18,522 --> 00:06:20,200
Lint can't see that.

114
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,480
So read your steps:

115
00:06:22,930 --> 00:06:25,726
all of them have the two lines, or none of them do.

116
00:06:26,926 --> 00:06:29,576
There's one step in the list, so I fly to the door.

117
00:06:30,476 --> 00:06:33,506
It's done, and paid, and here's the next.

118
00:06:34,406 --> 00:06:37,045
In through the Mouth, and through the ring.

119
00:06:37,495 --> 00:06:41,000
That's last lecture's recording calling, and I'll leave it for now.

120
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:44,874
Across the Nave and up the tunnel.

121
00:06:45,324 --> 00:06:48,876
The step is done again, and Rook is calling from the altar.

122
00:06:49,776 --> 00:06:53,233
On Science, I select the Altar, and there's my reading.

123
00:06:54,133 --> 00:06:57,222
On Comms, I play the rest, and I mark the Gallery.

124
00:06:59,022 --> 00:07:02,854
Back across the Nave, into the built room, and to the far end.

125
00:07:03,754 --> 00:07:07,898
That's the third step, and a second recording, at the top of the list.

126
00:07:08,798 --> 00:07:10,201
I take it aboard.

127
00:07:10,651 --> 00:07:11,691
And that's the game.

128
00:07:12,892 --> 00:07:13,894
Now it's your turn.

129
00:07:14,794 --> 00:07:16,544
Give the Altar a second tab.

130
00:07:17,444 --> 00:07:19,938
Add a fifth step that carries the bowl home.

131
00:07:20,838 --> 00:07:23,564
Give the crew a way to lose on purpose.

132
00:07:24,464 --> 00:07:26,884
Then break one line where lint can see it,

133
00:07:27,334 --> 00:07:28,709
and one where it can't.

134
00:07:30,509 --> 00:07:33,150
Next time, the crew goes outside.
